  "title": "Causal primitives: sufficiency and necessity",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "62fc5b5b-1fe2-4421-a648-bf574a8636bc",
      "text": "Measures of causation rest on two causal primitives: sufficiency, the certainty about an effect given a cause, and necessity, the certainty about a cause given an effect.",
